    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0136" n="126" xml:id="pg126"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 P. W./186</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-10">April 10, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador called to see me this afternoon at my request.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador gave me a copy of a secret memorandum<anchor n="60"
                        xml:id="d124-f1"/> containing information regarding British naval and
                    military forces at Singapore which he had prepared in response to a request made
                    by Secretary Hull. (I subsequently handed this memorandum to the Secretary
                    personally.)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d124-f1" n="60" xml:id="d124-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it indicated the British Government’s intentions to increase British
                    air strength in Malaya to 22 squadrons of 336 aircraft (846d.20/62).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
